rewritten-to-match: the timed decoder follows Crystal HuffDecode: the prepare step generates the test data and encodes it once (untimed, as Crystal does with the encoder prepare and run(0)); each round rebuilds the tree from the stored frequencies and decodes all bits MSB-first, emitting every leaf byte with no zero-byte filter (the original filter was not in Crystal). The tree queue tie-break now matches Crystal bsearch (before equal frequencies), which changes tree shape from the original. Prep mode runs only the warmup rounds. The original version is kept as compress_huffdecode_idiomatic.
